{"repositoryId":1426191655,"availability":"available","full":"skorotkiewicz/timestral-demo","name":"timestral-demo","description":"predicts future values","category":"Other","language":"HTML","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-19T21:18:47Z","updated":"2026-10-19T21:19:27Z","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":[],"demo":"https://huggingface.co/mistralai/Timestral-5M","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T22:20:12.850Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T22:20:12.850Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T22:20:12.850Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-19T22:20:12.850Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A tiny CPU demo for Mistral's Timestral-5M. Feed it past measurements and it predicts future values, including uncertainty. It needs no training on this example.","Requires uv. First run installs CPU-only PyTorch and downloads the model. Dependencies, model weights, and the virtual environment stay in this folder. Open forecast.html in your browser. It is self-contained, with zoom, pan, an overview slider, and clickable legends. You can also serve it with rala.","The default data simulates three weeks of hourly server traffic, then hides the following 48 hours from the model. The chart compares its forecast with the real held-out values and a baseline that repeats the previous day's traffic. MAE measures forecast error; lower is better. The shaded area is the model's 10th–90th percentile range. Its actual coverage on new data can differ from 80%. The timing covers one forecast call, excluding model loading and downloads."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/skorotkiewicz/timestral-demo/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"0196d7274f2608ce23073fd16ee72eb48963b30ab42fb35f0ea1815f9b841e9a","extractedAt":"2026-10-19T22:20:12.929Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T22:20:12.929Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A tiny CPU demo for Mistral's Timestral-5M. Feed it past measurem